# Repository Handoff Governance

Before planning or editing `repos/ai-vault`, read its `.rules`, `CLAUDE.md`,
and `CONTRIBUTING.md`. Add their completion obligations to the task checklist.

Git inspection is read-only in every repository. Never run `git add`,
`git commit`, or `git push`.

After EXECUTE file changes, run `repos/ai-vault/scripts/commit_handoff.py
render` once per repository changed during the current agent generation. Pass
that repository with `--repo` and only attributed paths with repeated `--path`.
Paste each generated pair of Markdown blocks exactly:

1. One `git -C <repo> add -- <changed paths>` command.
2. One `git -C <repo> commit` command with exactly two `-m` flags.

The second `-m` value is one paragraph wrapped at 70 characters with no blank
line. Never use a HEREDOC or additional `-m` flags. Do not generate a handoff
for read-only turns, clean repositories, or external-only operations.
